        "original_id": "3e7182b5-9d0c-51d1-ad2b-33fb3887f48f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Awards: NHL Plus-Minus Award\n- Organizations: National Hockey League, Kontinental Hockey League\n- People: Pavel Datsyuk, Brad McCrimmon\n- Teams: SKA Saint Petersburg, Calgary\n- Topics: plus-minus statistics\n\nFacts:\n- In 1987–88, Brad McCrimmon was named a second-team All-Star, played in the 1988 NHL All-Star Game, and won the NHL Plus-Minus Award with a league-leading +48.\n- The NHL Plus-Minus Award was awarded annually by the National Hockey League to the ice hockey player who played at least 60 games and led the league in plus-minus statistics.\n- The NHL Plus-Minus Award was discontinued after it was awarded to Pavel Datsyuk following the season mentioned in the source.\n- Pavel Datsyuk, born on 20 July 1978, is a Russian professional ice hockey player known as The Magic Man and served as captain of SKA Saint Petersburg in the Kontinental Hockey League.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
