        "text": "Page: NHL Plus-Minus Award. Sentence: The NHL Plus-Minus Award was a trophy awarded annually by the National Hockey League to the ice hockey \"player, having played a minimum of 60 games, who leads the league in plus-minus statistics.\"\nPage: NHL Plus-Minus Award. Sentence: The Award was discontinued after being awarded to Pavel Datsyuk following the  season.\nPage: Pavel Datsyuk. Sentence: Pavel Valerievich Datsyuk (Russian: Па́вел Вале́рьевич Дацю́к , ] ; born 20 July 1978) also known as The Magic Man is a Russian professional ice hockey player and captain for SKA Saint Petersburg of the Kontinental Hockey League (KHL).\nPage: Brad McCrimmon. Sentence: He achieved his greatest success in Calgary, where he was named a second team All-Star in 1987–88, played in the 1988 NHL All-Star Game and won the Plus-Minus Award with a league leading total of +48.",
